From 43f5d107cfd19d3678a45a57b73c9a0980e7a702 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 06:50:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] man: State who marks a relay down after a BEGIN_DIR
 refusal

DoSBeginDirLimitEnabled's manual said every non-onion-service client
marks the relay not running. connection_dir_client_request_failed()
skips that for bridges, EntryNodes, and onion service requests. The
request still fails in every case.

Part of #41339.
---
 changes/begindir_man_client_impact |  5 +++++
 doc/man/tor.1.txt                  | 12 ++++++------
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 changes/begindir_man_client_impact

diff --git a/changes/begindir_man_client_impact b/changes/begindir_man_client_impact
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4bfd9de
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changes/begindir_man_client_impact
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+  o Documentation (man page):
+    - Say which clients mark a relay not running after
+      DoSBeginDirLimitEnabled refuses a BEGIN_DIR stream. Clients using
+      bridges or EntryNodes, and onion service requests, do not. Part of
+      ticket 41339.
diff --git a/doc/man/tor.1.txt b/doc/man/tor.1.txt
index 3ae1973..5d92cda 100644
--- a/doc/man/tor.1.txt
+++ b/doc/man/tor.1.txt
@@ -3113,12 +3113,12 @@ Denial of Service mitigation subsystem described above.
 [[DoSBeginDirLimitEnabled]] **DoSBeginDirLimitEnabled** **0**|**1**|**auto**::
 
     Refuse a BEGIN_DIR stream on a circuit that already has
-    DoSBeginDirMaxStreams open directory streams. Tor clients treat a refused
-    stream as a failed directory request and, except for onion service
-    requests, consider this relay down until their next consensus. Whatever
-    this value, such streams are counted on the MetricsPort. "auto" means use
-    the consensus parameter. If not defined in the consensus, the value is 0.
-    (Default: auto)
+    DoSBeginDirMaxStreams open directory streams. The client fails that
+    request. A client that is not using bridges or EntryNodes, and whose
+    request is not for an onion service, also marks this relay not running
+    until its next consensus. Whatever this value, such streams are counted
+    on the MetricsPort. "auto" means use the consensus parameter. If not
+    defined in the consensus, the value is 0. (Default: auto)
 
 [[DoSBeginDirMaxStreams]] **DoSBeginDirMaxStreams** __NUM__::
 
